{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Sarah denied, saying</b> — I am astonished at the righteous prophetess: how could she deny what HaShem said to the prophet, and also, why did she not believe the words of the angels of Elohim? And what appears right in my eyes is that these angels who appeared as men came to Abraham, and he in his wisdom recognized them, and they announced to him: \"I will return to you and to Sarah a son,\" and Sarah was listening but did not know that they were angels of the Most High, as in the case of Manoah's wife (Judges 13:6), and perhaps she did not see them at all. <b>And she laughed within herself</b> — in mockery, as in \"He who sits in heaven, YHWH laughs; HaShem mocks at them\" (Psalms 2:4), for laughter that expresses joy is in the mouth: \"Then our mouth will be filled with laughter\" (Psalms 126:2), but laughter in the heart is not said of joy. And the Holy One, blessed be He, reproached her through Abraham: why was the matter impossible in her eyes, when it was fitting for her to believe or to say \"Amen, so may HaShem do.\" Now Abraham said to her: why did you laugh, is anything too wondrous for YHWH — but he did not explain to her that HaShem had revealed her secret to him, and she out of fear of Abraham denied it, for she thought that Abraham from recognizing her face would say thus, or because she was silent and did not give praise and thanksgiving for the matter and did not rejoice. And he said: \"No, but you did laugh.\" Then she understood that this was said to him in prophecy, and she was silent and did not answer him anything. And it is fitting to say further that Abraham did not reveal to her what was said to him at first (Genesis 17:19): \"But Sarah your wife will bear you a son\" — perhaps he waited until HaShem would send the tidings to her the next day, for he knew \"that HaShem Elohim does nothing unless He reveals His secret to His servants the prophets\" (Amos 3:7), or from his great alacrity in the commandments he was occupied with the matter at hand and with the affairs of the many people who were in his household, and afterward in his weariness he sat at the entrance of the tent, and the angels came before he had told her anything:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:22.671681783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}